ocedures Program Accreditations Quality Enhancement Plan SACSCOC Accreditation Reports SACSCOC Principles SACSCOC Correspondence Strategic Plan Strategic Plan Progress Reports Strategic Planning Policy Student Achievement Data Substantive Change Policy Surveys University Data and Reports WEAVE Approved Academic Program CIP Codes Self-Studies and Compliance Certification Office of the Bursar Arrow How to Make a Payment Online Nelnet Refunds 1098-T Collections of Accounts Receivable Student Health Insurance Withdrawals Important Dates Office of Computing & Information Services Arrow Meet the Staff Marketing, Communications & Workforce Development Arrow Alumni Career and Professional Development Government Relations Marketing and Communications Event Management Purchasing Arrow E-Verify Vendor Info Resources A-Z Index News The Beep Blog Calendar Campus Map Faculty and Staff Directory Arrow Back Resources For Future Roadrunners Adult Learners Veterans Dual Enrollment Current Roadrunners Parents and Guardians Alumni Faculty and Staff Community and Business Online Education Mountain Campus Event Management La Comunidad Hispanohablante Roadrunner Scholars Program Resources A-Z Index Roadrunner Portal Email Academic Calendar Georgia VIEW Faculty CV and Syllabi News Event Calendar Community Events Campus Map The Beep Blog Disability Access Policies and Procedures Title IX Search results for Search Home Home Home Arrow About Arrow Marketing, Communications & Workforce Development Arrow Career and Professional Development Arrow Career and Professional Development Left Arrow Back To Marketing, Communications & Workforce Development Welcome to Career & Professional Development! Please see the array of events and services available to students and alumni. August Fall 2026 events coming soon! September Fall 2026 events coming soon! October Fall 2026 events coming soon! November Fall 2026 events coming soon! Frequently Asked Questions If I’m looking for a job, where do I start? Handshake! https://bit.ly/HandshakeDSC This is the “Indeed” for Dalton State students and alumni!  Download the app and activate your account today!  On Handshake, you can search for jobs, apply to jobs/internships, and even register to attend events, webinars, and workshops.  Students can even contact employers directly to learn more about their companies and opportunities.  All jobs and internships, both on and off campus, are located on Handshake. Where can I practice my interview skills? You have great options to prepare with confidence! One of the best tools available to you is Big Interview, Dalton State’s free online interview training system. With Big Interview, you can: -Complete mock interviews tailored to your major or career field -Record and review your responses -Practice using the S.T.A.R. Method -Follow step-by-step video and written lessons -Share your recordings with a trusted mentor, professor, or Career Advisor for feedback Access Big Interview here: https://daltonstate.biginterview.com/members/interview_dashboard/ Prefer in-person practice? You can also schedule a mock interview with your Career Advisor for personalized feedback and coaching. Schedule an appointment today: https://bit.ly/DSCareerAppt What is the name of the book with information for interviewing? That is the ever-popular Career Guide.  You can pick up a paper copy in the Dean of Students Office located in the Pope Student Center or access it virtually HERE! https://www.flipsnack.com/96F9B6CC5A8/official-dalton-state-career-guide-2025-2026/full-view.html Do you have aptitude tests if I am not sure which major I want to student? Yes, Focus2 Career is designed to help you explore your career options and can aid in decision making when it comes to selecting a major or career.  This assessment is self-guided and requires an access code that you can access on Handshake under “Library Resources” to complete. You are encouraged, however, to schedule an appointment with a Career Advisor to help you delve into the information and explore your options.  Schedule an appointment HERE! https://bit.ly/DSCareerAppt When is a good time to start researching and applying to graduate school? It’s never too early to talk about graduate school and what you need to be doing now to prepare.  Please schedule an appointment with a Career Advisor today to get started on that journey. https://bit.ly/DSCareerAppt What is “Stepping Blocks?” SteppingBlocks is a career exploration tool, like a digital Career Counselor.  Use your Single-Sign-On (SSO) to sign-in and start exploring today! https://daltonstate.steppingblocks.com Internships: How do internships work? Obtaining an internship is a great way to receive real-world, work experience while gaining a glimpse into your future profession.  Internships typically last for a short duration but can boost your resume and tip the scales in helping you secure a good job in the future.  Some departments on campus require internships, and credit is given just like a class. Regardless, all students can benefit from internship experience, and it can be independent of your school or department.  Some internships pay and others do not. To search for an internship, you can go to almost any job search and type in ‘internship’.  Want to increase your chances of landing an impressive internship?  Check out Handshake.  You can also plan to attend one of our upcoming Career Events (listed above) in the fall or spring. Can you help me create and/or update my resume or cover letter? We need to change it to this: Yes! You have several resources to help you build strong, professional documents. Start by reviewing the Dalton State Career Guide for formatting tips and sample résumés and cover letters. You can also use Big Interview’s Résumé Builder to create a résumé from scratch or upload and organize one you’ve already created https://daltonstate.biginterview.com/members/dashboard Once you’ve drafted your materials, schedule an appointment with a Career Advisor or email us. We’ll review your résumé or cover letter and help you tailor it to your target career, internship, or graduate program. Schedule an appointment here: https://bit.ly/DSCareerAppt How do I learn more about and apply for an undergraduate research opportunity? Please contact Carole Shealy [email protected] to learn more about your options and how to apply. If I want to work on campus, where do I start? There are several work study (campus jobs) opportunities each fall and spring. Start on Handshake!  All work study positions will be posted there.  If you find one you like, apply for it.  The campus employer will reach out if they want to interview you.  Remember, in order to work on campus, you must be eligible through Financial Aid.  If you’re unsure, please contact Financial Aid. About Us Career & Professional Development Mission Statement Career & Professional Development serves our students and alumni through expanding their knowledge and skills by providing them with comprehensive career related resources which empowers them to attain short- and long-term professional goals. Meet the Staff Mallory Safley Director for Career and Professional Development Phone icon 706-272-2997 Email [email protected] Kelsey Riner Coordinator of Career & Professional Development Phone icon 706-272-4411 Email [email protected] Have questions? We’d be happy to answer your questions about our Career and Development services. Please reach out through the contact information listed above. Schedule an Appointment Contact Us Phone icon 706-272-4428 Email [email protected] Map Icon Dean of Students Office, Pope Student Center Map Marker 650 College Drive Dalton, GA 30720 Phone Icon (706) 272-4436 More Information A - Z Index Campus Map Accreditation Consumer Information Title IX Employment Request Info Schedule Tour ©  2026  Dalton State College Human Trafficking Notice Ethics Hotline XML Sitemap Privacy Policy Close"
    },
